Article 4 Where a party or an interested person of a notarized matter provides evidence proving that the notarization institution or its notary falls under any of the following circumstances in notarization activities, the People's Court shall determine that the notarization institution is at fault:
(1) issuing a notarization certificate for untrue or unlawful matters;
(2) damaging or altering a notarization certificate or notarization archives;
(3) disclosing trade secrets or personal privacy known in the course of practice;
(4) issuing a notarization certificate in violation of notarization procedures, notarization rules, and industry standards formulated by the judicial administration department of the State Council;
(5) failing to fulfill the full obligation of examination and verification during the notarization process, resulting in an erroneous or untrue notarization certificate;
(6) failing to correct or remedy an erroneous notarization certificate upon application of the party or interested person of the notarized matter;
(7) other circumstances in violation of laws, regulations, or mandatory provisions of the judicial administration department of the State Council.
